        "## 6. Conclusions & Recommendations\n",
        "\n",
        "> **Note on confidence:** Findings 1 and 5 are based on large, clear gaps\n",
        "> on a sample of 90,000 orders, so the pattern is very unlikely to be\n",
        "> random. Findings 2, 3, and 4 are based on smaller gaps (under 7%)\n",
        "> across multiple groups, which have not been statistically tested —\n",
        "> they are preliminary observations, not confirmed conclusions.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Finding 1 (strong evidence):** Discounts cost 12.3M (24.9% of gross\n",
        "revenue), but the correlation between discount size and order value is\n",
        "-0.0003 — essentially zero, measured directly across 90,000 orders.\n",
        "**Meaning:** The business is paying a large discount cost without any\n",
        "measurable increase in order size.\n",
        "**Recommendation:** Run a small-scale A/B test — reduce discounts for a\n",
        "sample of customers and compare their order value and order count to the\n",
        "rest, before changing the policy for everyone.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Finding 2 (preliminary):** Daily revenue varies by about 4% across\n",
        "months, with no obvious upward or downward trend.\n",
        "**Meaning:** Performance looks stable, but with only 9 months of data,\n",
        "this is not enough to rule out real seasonality.\n",
        "**Recommendation:** Keep tracking daily revenue month by month, and\n",
        "revisit this once a full year or more of data is available. Do not\n",
        "conclude the business is fully seasonality-free yet.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Finding 3 (preliminary):** The top category (Movies) beats the bottom\n",
        "one (Automotive) by 6.7%, and beats the average by 3.1%, out of 24\n",
        "categories.\n",
        "**Meaning:** No category looks clearly dominant, but a 6.7% gap across\n",
        "24 groups has not been tested for statistical significance, and could\n",
        "reflect a smaller real difference hidden inside random variation.\n",
        "**Recommendation:** Do not defund, discontinue, or over-invest in any\n",
        "single category based on this gap alone. A formal test (ANOVA) is\n",
        "needed before treating any category as meaningfully stronger or weaker.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Finding 4 (preliminary):** Average order value differs by under 1%\n",
        "across age groups and genders.\n",
        "**Meaning:** The gap is small enough to look negligible, but this has\n",
        "not been formally tested, so it should not be treated as final proof\n",
        "that no group differs.\n",
        "**Recommendation:** Do not prioritize marketing spend by age or gender\n",
        "based on order value alone; if a future test confirms a real gap, that\n",
        "would justify targeting, but there is not enough evidence for it yet.\n",
